# Git Workflow for Parallel PRs and Agents

## Prefer temporary full clones over worktrees

For parallel PR work, use **isolated clones** (e.g. `/tmp/iptv-proxy-v2-pr-<short-name>` with their own `.git`). Push to `origin` from the clone; do not share `.git/objects` across parallel agents.

Main repo `/home/benklop/repos/iptv-proxy-v2`: user integration only — avoid agent commits when possible.

## Worktrees only when necessary

If worktrees are required:

- **Max 2** active linked worktrees on one repo
- **One mutating git operation at a time** per repo (commit, rebase, merge, fetch+prune, worktree add/remove)
- Parallel read-only ops (status, diff, tests) are OK

## Cleanup after PR completion

- `git worktree remove <path>` when PR pushed/merged
- `git worktree prune`
- `git branch -d <branch>` if merged locally
- `rm -rf /tmp/iptv-proxy-v2-pr-*` when clone work is done

## Never do as "repair"

- Do NOT delete `.git/worktrees/*/index` or `.git/index` casually
- Do NOT use `git commit --no-verify` unless the user explicitly requests it
- Do NOT treat fsck "missing blob" as full re-clone when multiple worktrees exist — check per-worktree `git status` first

## Diagnosis order when git errors

1. `git worktree list`
2. `git -C <failing-path> status`
3. Fix failing worktree only (remove/recreate from `origin/<branch>`) OR use a fresh clone
4. `git fsck --full` only after worktrees are healthy

## Example clone workflow

```bash
git clone git@github.com:klopstack/iptv-proxy-v2.git /tmp/iptv-proxy-v2-pr-foo
cd /tmp/iptv-proxy-v2-pr-foo
git checkout -b feature/foo origin/main
# edit, commit, push
rm -rf /tmp/iptv-proxy-v2-pr-foo  # when done
```
